{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. I understand you came in today because of a bad headache and high blood pressure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. My blood pressure was 220 over 110 at my doctor’s office. The headache has been going on for over a week—it’s like my usual migraines, but much worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You mentioned it's a throbbing pain in the front of your head and you're sensitive to light?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. No nausea or vomiting this time, but it’s constant and exhausting. I even had a brief episode of weakness on my right side a week ago, but the neurologist cleared me then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks for that. We’ve reviewed your records. You have a history of migraines, high blood pressure from primary hyperaldosteronism, pseudotumor cerebri, and sleep apnea—all of which can play a role here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, and my blood pressure has been hard to control. I’ve tried several meds, but they make me feel tired or too low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:11:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you’re on amlodipine and propranolol. We gave you labetalol in the ER to bring your pressure down. Your CT scan of the head was normal—no bleeding or stroke."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. But the headache is still really bad. The Dilaudid helped a little more than morphine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to keep monitoring your blood pressure and pain. We also did a chest X-ray and EKG—both were stable. No signs of heart strain or fluid in the lungs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did have chest tightness on the train this morning. It went to my left shoulder, but no sweating or shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your cardiac enzymes three times—no sign of a heart attack. Given your normal stress test and angiogram in the past, it’s likely not cardiac. Probably related to anxiety or muscle tension."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ve been under a lot of stress lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adding captopril to help control your blood pressure. It’s a different type of blood pressure med that might work better with your hyperaldosteronism."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve taken lisinopril before and it made me so tired. I had to stop it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Captopril is similar, but we’ll start low and monitor. If it causes fatigue, we’ll switch to enalapril, which you might tolerate better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2140-02-03 18:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds fair."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood pressure is coming down—now 158 over 90. But you’re still having headaches?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, still pretty bad. I’m taking the Tylenol and oxycodone, but it’s not fully helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Neurology reviewed your case. Since your headache didn’t improve with blood pressure control and your eye exam is normal, it’s unlikely to be pseudotumor cerebri."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s still a migraine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. But we can’t use triptans because you’re on Celexa and have heart risk factors. NSAIDs are out because of your allergy. So we’re sticking with Tylenol and short-term oxycodone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I wish there was something more effective. The nasal Stadol my old neurologist used to prescribe helped a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We looked into that. Unfortunately, it’s very expensive and not covered under your plan. We’ll get you an appointment with your former neurologist to discuss long-term options."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that would be good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, your EKG shows a prolonged QT interval. You’re on three medications that can affect this: Celexa, Topamax, and tizanidine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Tizanidine is for muscle spasms in my neck. I take it at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think the benefits of Celexa and Topamax outweigh the risks, so we’re going to stop the tizanidine to protect your heart rhythm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that safe? I rely on it for sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor you. If the spasms come back, we can try other options. But your heart rhythm is a bigger concern right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2140-02-04 08:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I trust you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2140-02-04 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure is now 132 over 84—much better. And your headache is improving?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2140-02-04 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, definitely better since last night. I’m still taking the oxycodone, but less often."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2140-02-04 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re going to switch you from captopril to enalapril once a day. It’s the same class but easier to take and less likely to cause fatigue for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2140-02-04 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And what about the propranolol? I remember you said my heart rate was slow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2140-02-04 14:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your heart rate was in the 50s. We held the propranolol for now. We’ll restart it once daily instead of twice, since it also helps prevent migraines."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2140-02-04 14:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That sounds okay. I don’t want to feel dizzy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Your blood pressure has been stable between 110 and 130 over 80. Your discharge is approved for today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good news. What meds will I be going home on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting enalapril once daily for blood pressure, stopping tizanidine, and reducing propranolol to once daily. You’ll take Tylenol as needed and a short course of oxycodone—just four days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds—like Topamax and acetazolamide?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue those. They help with migraines and pseudotumor cerebri. Your PCP has been updated on all changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have a follow-up with my neurologist soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve scheduled you with Dr. ___ next week to review your headache management and consider other treatments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I feel much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Keep monitoring your blood pressure at home, take your meds as directed, and call if the headache worsens or you have any chest pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for explaining everything so clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Our team is here for you. You’ll receive discharge instructions and prescriptions at the desk. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2140-02-05 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2140-02-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a quick check before you leave. How are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2140-02-05 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. Headache is mild now, and I’m not feeling dizzy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2140-02-05 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Blood pressure is 116 over 80—excellent. You’re cleared to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2140-02-05 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad this is behind me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2140-02-05 10:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy, keep your follow-ups, and reach out if anything changes. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2140-02-05 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2140-02-03 17:49:00",
    "admission_end": "2140-02-05 17:28:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of primary hyperaldosteronism, migraines, pseudotumor cerebri, obstructive sleep apnea, and hypertension was admitted for headache and hypertensive urgency with blood pressure up to 220/110. Imaging showed no acute intracranial or pulmonary process. Her headache persisted despite blood pressure control, and neurologic evaluation ruled out pseudotumor cerebri and hypertensive emergency, leading to a diagnosis of severe migraine. Blood pressure was managed with captopril initially, then transitioned to enalapril for better tolerability. Propranolol was reduced due to bradycardia, and tizanidine was discontinued due to QT prolongation risk. Headache improved with acetaminophen and short-term oxycodone. She was discharged home with medication adjustments and follow-up scheduled with neurology for ongoing headache management.",
    "problems": [
      "Migraine, unspecified, without mention of intractable migraine without mention of status migrainosus",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Benign intracranial hypertension",
      "Hyperaldosteronism, unspecified",
